 			<p>For a fortnight, the Professor came and went with lover-like regularity; then he stayed away for three whole days, and made no sign⁠—a proceeding which caused everybody to look sober, and Jo to become pensive, at first, and then⁠—alas for romance!⁠—very cross.</p>
 			<p>“Disgusted, I dare say, and gone home as suddenly as he came. It’s nothing to me, of course; but I <em>should</em> think he would have come and bid us goodbye, like a gentleman,” she said to herself, with a despairing look at the gate, as she put on her things for the customary walk, one dull afternoon.</p>
